Apple is working with German confectionary brand Ritter Sport to offer a unique <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/apple-music/">Apple Music</a> promotion.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/02/apple-music-ritter-sport.jpeg" alt="" width="1200" height="675" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-1037865" /><br/>
The collaboration, branded as "Limited Edition Ritter Sport x &zwnj;Apple Music&zwnj;," involves promoting iconic albums on Ritter Sport's iconic 100g square chocolate bars (via <em><a href="https://www.macerkopf.de/2026/02/27/ritter-sport-limited-edition-apple/">Macerkopf</a></em>). There will be a QR code on the back of each bar that links directly to the album on &zwnj;Apple Music&zwnj; and provides a free trial subscription to the service. <br/>
<br/>
Ritter Sport and &zwnj;Apple Music&zwnj; have selected five albums that have shaped German music history across different genres, including Cro's "RAOP," Marteria's "Happy for the Future II," Scorpions' "Crazy World," Sarah Connor's "Mother Tongue," and Helene Fischer's "Farbenspiel," for the series. They are each available on &zwnj;Apple Music&zwnj; in Dolby Atmos.<br/>
<br/>
